The Customized Statistical Performance Indicator (SPI) comprises the following subset of WB's SPI that correspond to activities supported by the Project: 
â€¢	Pillar 1- Data use (dimension 1.5 on use by international bodies): (i) Comparable poverty headcount ratios at $1.90 a day (or updated line), (ii) Labor force participation rate by sex and age (%); 
â€¢	Pillar 2 - Data services (dimension 2. on online access): (iii) ODIN open data openness score; 
â€¢	Pillar 4 - Data sources (dimension 4.1 on censuses and surveys): (iv) Population & Housing Census, (v) Agriculture census, (vi) Household Survey on income / expenditures, (vii) Labor Force Survey; 
â€¢	Pillar 5 - Data infrastructures (dimension 5.1 on legislation and governance): (viii) Legislation indicator based on PARIS21 indicators on SDG 17.18.2.
